Steve Leferve wrote on Sun, 2 May 2004 14:26:45 -0400 in article 
news:<c73eh9$700$1@charm.magnus.acs.ohio-state.edu>:
> What are the most valuable rings? Is there a difference between rings you
> value in the early game and rings you value in the late game?

Conflict is the most all-around useful.  In the end game, Free Action is a 
little better, though you should certainly wear both if you have them.

Regeneration is excellent in the early game but worthless by the end.

Teleport Control is great until you get it naturally.

Slow digestion is overrated -- don't bother unless you are a Wizard.

Poison Resistance is great if you start with it, since it will let you get 
the intrinsic quickly, risk-free.

The other rings are mostly useless.

